append overview
  p: strong Summary:
  ul.summary
    li.
      Collaborated with #[+link("https://www.metacreation.net/philippepasquier/home") Dr. Philippe Pasquier] and
      #[+link("https://www.metacreation.net/team/arshia-sobhan") Arshia Sobhan] at the
      #[+link("https://www.metacreation.net/") Metacreation Lab] to train and deploy a #[abbr GAN] using
      #[+link("https://www.metacreation.net/autolume") Autolume-Live] for real-time image generation.
    li.
      Wrangled and preprocessed dataset of abstract artwork from artist and late grandfather,
      #[+link("https://voormeij.ca/") Peter John Voormeij].
    li.
      Designed and implemented a Unity-based #[abbr VR] environment and built a communication pipeline using Open
      Sound Control and Network Device Interface protocols for live model interaction.
    li.
      Conducted qualitative evaluation of #[abbr GAN] model outputs to assess visual coherence and latent space
      behaviour.

  section#abstract
    +h(3, "Abstract")
    p.introduction.
      AutolumeGallery is an interactive virtual gallery space where users can manipulate and explore the latent space
      of a #[abbr GAN] in 3D. A canvas receives artwork generated in real-time from Autolume-Live, influenced by the
      position and rotation of several objects in the virtual environment. Users can use these "manipulators" to alter
      the piece and take an active role in its creation and appearance. The #[abbr GAN] model was trained on the
      abstract artwork of my late grandfather, Peter John Voormeij, as my way of honouring and connecting with his work.

  section#demo
    +h(3, "Demo")
    div.youtube-container
      iframe(
        src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/Brn7nG2WOXA?si=ApqnHnHsTaW3ukRk&rel=0&hl=en-ca"
        title="AutolumeGallery - Demo Video"
